---
description: Headless-first Pincushion AI critique for a complete review surface
alwaysApply: false
---

Ask for the page URL if none was supplied. Treat the request as a one-off Crit.

Before capture, read `get_project_context({ url, view: "critic" })`.
Write its same-origin registered `urls` array to a local JSON file and
pass it as `--inventory`; the helper also discovers links and sitemaps.

1. Start headlessly with `node <pincushion-mcp>/scripts/capture-snapshot.mjs --critique <url> <outputDir> [--inventory=<registered-urls-json-file>] [--page-only] [--require-auth] [--pins=<json-or-file>]`.
   Require bounded `mode: 'critique-v1'` JSON, status, discovery, every page,
   desktop/mobile `imagePath`, `pinPositions`, `hotspots`, and visible semantic
   evidence. Default discovery max 64; use `--page-only` only when explicitly
   requested.
2. Read existing pins with
   `get_annotations({ projectId, pageUrls, view: "critique", critiqueRunId? })`.
   Review every discovered screen, rank the top 8 findings across the run, and
   keep at most 3 per screen. Use unique visible selectors, concrete fixes, and
   no duplicates.
3. Make one `critiqueRunId`, use it on every pin, and set `visibility` to
   `"public"` for a public route or `"project_members"` for a signed-in app.
   Re-read by run ID and keep the exact pin IDs.
4. Final-capture with `--pins=<json-or-file>` after creation. By default call
   `generate_critique_report` with `purpose: "critique"`, the matching
   `accessMode`, `coverage`, `critiqueRunId`, exact `critiquePinIds`, and `screens`. For zero
   good findings, use `purpose: "capture"`, label “no AI findings”, and still
   return the review surface.

Public pages are headless. Use a headed browser only for initial sign-in via
`snapshot --login` or a flow unavailable to headless capture. Do not label
incomplete coverage complete or publish private pixels/findings publicly.
Preserve Pincushion’s native report and brand presentation. Shared images and
pin records leave the machine when published; auth state does not. Keep pins
visible, concrete, actionable, and on-brand; omit generic UX advice.
